{% extends "../_guide.njk" %}

{% block guideContent %}
  <p class="govuk-body">If you tell us you want to take part, this is what will happen:</p>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>At the time you booked, we will call you on the phone number you gave us. The call will come from +44 20 3443 8791.</li>
    <li>Two people from our team will be on the call. One person will ask questions. The other person will write down what you say. So that we don't miss anything important, the call system will also transcribe the call. This means it will turn the words we say into text. It doesn't save any sound.</li>
    <li>We will explain the research and what you are saying yes to. You can then ask any questions.</li>
    <li>If you are happy to take part, we will ask you questions. If not, you can end the call.</li>
    <li>We will first ask you some questions about [what questions you'll ask first]. Then we will ask you about [what questions you'll ask next].</li>
    <li>At the end, we will remind you what we will do next. We will also tell you how you can ask us to delete anything you told us.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">If you agree to take part, what you are saying yes to</h3>

  <p class="govuk-body">If you say on the call that you agree to take part you are saying you understand that:</p>

  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>Taking part is your choice. Nothing will happen if you decide not to or tell us what you don't like.</li>
    <li>You don't have to tell us anything you don't want to.</li>
    <li>We will not save a sound recording of the call. The call system will transcribe the call. This means it will turn the words we say into text. We will take out anything you say that could show it was you who gave the feedback. For example, names, places or information related to your probation.</li>
    <li>We will only share information that could identify you and what you said outside of the Ministry of Justice if someone might be at risk, or if the law says we must. For example, if you tell us that:
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>you plan to hurt yourself</li>
        <li>you plan to hurt someone else</li>
        <li>you plan to commit a crime</li>
      </ul>
      If this happens, we may need to report it to keep people safe.
    </li>
    <li>We may share what we learn publicly, but not who said it.</li>
    <li>We will keep the information you share in this feedback call that doesn't identify you only for as long as we need it. A record that you took part in this research that includes your name, and phone number will be deleted within 2 years. Sometimes your information may be stored in countries outside the European Economic Area (EEA).</li>
    <li>You can change your mind about taking part, even after the call. You can ask us to delete what you told us by emailing us at <a class="govuk-link" href="mailto:probation-research@justice.gov.uk">probation-research@justice.gov.uk</a>.</li>
    <li>If you'd like more information about how we'll use your information and your rights, you can <a class="govuk-link" href="#">read our privacy notice for user research participants</a>.</li>
  </ul>
{% endblock %}
